hadiths[13]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2859","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “There are three rights that God has a duty to appoint: offices The one who wants to perform, the one who strives in the cause of God, and the one who is married wants to be chaste. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2859 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2860","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Al-Walid Hisham bin Abdul-Malik told us, Amr bin Thabit, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sahl bin Hanif, that Sahl narrated to him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever helps a Mujahideen in the cause of God, or a fighter, or a debtor in his hardship, or one who is oppressed by his neck, God will give him shade in His shade. “On the Day when there will be no shade except His shade.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2860 - Rather, Amr Rafidi is abandoned"
"2861","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar al-Adl told me, saying: Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Abu Naim Al-Fadl bin Dukain, Issa bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Sulami told us, Talha Al-Yami told us, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin A single man, may God be pleased with him, said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, teach me something that will admit me to Paradise. He said: “If you shorten the sermon, you will have removed the issue, freed the spirit, and freed the slave.” He said: Aren’t they one? He said: “For the freedom of a soul is to be set apart by freeing it, and the freeing of a slave is to determine its price, and the gift entrusted, and the fay’ are upon the kin. The oppressor. If you cannot bear that, then feed the hungry, give drink to the thirsty, enjoin what is right, and forbid evil. If you cannot bear that, then desist. “Your tongue is only of good.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2861 - True"
"2862","Abu Al-Qasim Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Asim Ibn Sulaiman, and Ali Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, on the authority of Salman, may God be pleased with him, who said: I wrote to my family to plant five One hundred shoots, and if they become stuck, I am free. So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that to him, and he said: “Plant, and stipulate for them. So if you want to plant something, let me know.” Then he came and started to plant it, except for one, which I planted with my own hand, and all of them stuck except for one. “This is an authentic hadith.” From the hadith of Asim bin Sulaiman Al-Ahwal, according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2862 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2863","Maymoon bin Ishaq Al-Hashimi told us, in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Amr bin Asim Al-Kalabi told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Abbas Al-Jariri, Amr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Which of the offices He was appointed for a thousand uqiyahs, and he paid for them as nothing but ten uqiyahs, so he is a slave, and for any one who was appointed, he was appointed for a hundred dinars, so he paid for them for nothing but ten dinars. “He is a slave.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2863 - True"
"2864","Ahmad bin Salman bin Al-Hasan Al-Najjad Al-Faqih told us, dictating in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Makram Al-Bazzaz told us, Othman bin Omar told us, Ali bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decided In the offices of the freed man, he must pay the blood money of a freed man according to what was paid from him.” Yahya said: Ikrimah said: On the authority of Ibn Abbas, “the punishment of the slave will be carried out on him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2864 - Aban followed it according to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2865","Abu al-Nadr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Faqih told us, Uthman ibn Sa`id al-Darimi and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us, they said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim, Aban bin Yazid told us, Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The one who has been freed will be fulfilled according to what is freed from him, on the account of the freeman, and whatever is enslaved, on the account of the slave.” This is an authentic hadith, subject to the condition. Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2866","Ibrahim bin Asmah told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, and Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydalani told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, they said: Musa told us Ibn Ismail, Hammad Ibn Salama told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If someone is appointed to the decree, or inherits an inheritance, then he inherits in proportion to what he was freed from, and the guardianship is made over him in proportion to what he was freed from.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2866 - True"
"2867","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Saghani told us in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, He said: Nabhan, the office of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with him, told me. He said: I will drive with it to Al-Baida or Al-Abwa. She said: Who is this? I said: I am Nabhan, and she said: I left the rest of your letter to my nephew Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah. I helped him with him in His marriage. He said: So I said: No, by God, I will never do it to him. She said: If your oath is to enter upon me or see me, then by God you will never see me. I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “If there is someone at the office who is serving, hide yourself from him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2867 - True"
"2868","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Bakr Al-Hanafi told us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abdullah bin Wahb, on the authority of Tamim al-Dari, may God be pleased with him, that he said: O Messenger of God, a man from the polytheists greets the man at the hands of Muslim, he said: “He is more deserving of it in his life and death.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration on the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and Abdullah bin Wahb bin Zam’ah is well known, and his witness is on the authority of Tamim al-Dari, the hadith of Qubaisa bin Dhu’ayb
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2868 - This is what only Ibn Majah narrated, then it is a second illusion from Al-Hakim, as Ibn Zam’a did not narrate on the authority of Tamim Al-Darimi, and Abdullah bin Mawhib corrected him."
"2869","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Mushar Abd Al-A’la bin Mushar Al-Saghani told us, he told me Yahya bin Hamza Al-Hadrami, Abdul Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abdullah bin Wahb Al-Qurashi told us, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Dhu’ayb, on the authority of Tamim al-Dari, may God be pleased with him, who said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a man who greets another man, and he said: “He is He is more deserving of his life and death.”"
"2870","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the Martyr told us, Musaddad told us, Ismail bin Aliya told us, On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Awf, may God be pleased with him, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I witnessed a boy with my aunts swearing an oath to be pure, and I am not pleased that I have the red camels, and that I break them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2870 - True"
"2871","Ali bin Abdul Rahman Al-Subaie informed us, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Zakaria bin Abi told us Zaida, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr bin Mutim, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “There is no swearing in Islam, and whatever swearing was made during pre-Islamic times, Islam only made it more difficult.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2871 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim
 The Book of Interpretation “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, we have begun in this book with the revelation of the Qur’an, in what was narrated in the Musnad from the readings, and it was mentioned The companions who compiled the Qur’an and memorized it, this is before interpretation. The Surah”"
